{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#121","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#121","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#121\",\"parent_revision\":\"ff1f9a2d9520fcd85afd00aec7ec6397df0b6a57ed69f120cf7f7682843396e8\",\"root_revision\":\"ff1f9a2d9520fcd85afd00aec7ec6397df0b6a57ed69f120cf7f7682843396e8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`[tool.ruff]` sets `fix = true` and `unsafe-fixes = true`. Under ruff 0.16, `RUF105` (noqa-comments) migrates `# noqa: XXX` to `# ruff: ignore[rule-name]`. At `packages/skilllint/boundary/plugin_agent_pa001_ingest.py:114` the autofix **deletes** the comment outright:\\n\\n```python\\n# noqa: PLC0415 \u2014 breaks import cycle\\n```\\n\\nBoth the suppression and the rationale go, leaving `import-outside-top-level` newly exposed. Sibling call sites in `as_series.py` convert correctly, so this one line is genuinely mangled rather than merely churned.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`RUF105` and `RUF201` are both in `lint.ignore` as of #107, so nothing is silently rewriting suppressions today. That is a deliberate hold, not a fix.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Decision This Defers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMigrating 34 suppressions from `# noqa` to ruff-proprietary `# ruff: ignore[...]` is a repo-wide call worth making on purpose rather than absorbing through a dependency bump. `# noqa` is also the portable form across tools.\\n\\nWhoever takes the migration: restore the `PLC0415` suppression by hand afterward, since the autofix eats it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #107 \u2014 where this surfaced\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"38aefb119565e96686aafeafc3bba236a4cdf8df739e3086042d1e44572f3858\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP_Bqw\"}"}